UnitFundsLib::push
├── when the recipient is any address
│   ├── it should transfer _amount to _recipient
│   └── it should not track _token
├── when the native mirror amount exceeds the batch balance
│   └── it should revert with InsufficientBalance for the native mirror token
├── when the native mirror amount equals the batch balance
│   ├── it should transfer the amount
│   └── it should not track the token
├── when a lower decimals mirror amount exceeds the batch native floored to the mirror decimals
│   └── it should revert with InsufficientBalance for the native mirror token
└── when a lower decimals mirror amount fits the batch native floored to the mirror decimals
    ├── it should transfer the amount
    └── it should not track the token

UnitFundsLib::pull
└── when pulling from the logical sender
    ├── it should pull _amount from the logical sender to the execution address
    └── it should track _token

UnitFundsLib::pay
├── when the payer is the execution address
│   ├── it should transfer _amount to _recipient
│   └── it should not track _token
├── when the payer is the logical sender
│   ├── it should transfer _amount from the logical sender to _recipient
│   └── it should not track _token
├── when the payer is neither the execution address nor the logical sender
│   └── it should revert with InvalidPayer
└── when the payer is the zero address and the logical sender is unset
    └── it should revert with InvalidPayer

UnitFundsLib::fund
├── given the payer is external
│   ├── when the spend mode is not amount
│   │   └── it should revert with InvalidSpendMode
│   └── given the spend mode is amount
│       ├── when the transfer delivers the full amount
│       │   └── it should return _spend.value as _amount
│       └── when the token charges a fee on transfer
│           └── it should return the received balance delta as _amount
└── when the payer is not external
    ├── it should resolve _spend against the execution address balance as _amount
    └── it should track _token

UnitFundsLib::resolveSpend
├── given the spend mode is amount
│   ├── when the requested value exceeds the balance
│   │   └── it should revert with InsufficientBalance for _asset
│   ├── when the requested value is within the balance
│   │   └── it should return _spend.value as _amount
│   ├── when the requested mirror value exceeds the batch balance within the raw mirror balance
│   │   └── it should revert with InsufficientBalance for the native mirror token
│   └── when the requested mirror value equals the batch balance
│       └── it should return the batch balance as _amount
└── given the spend mode is pips
    ├── when the pip value exceeds the denominator
    │   └── it should revert with InvalidPips for _spend.value
    └── given the pip value is within the denominator
        ├── when the pip proportion is positive
        │   └── it should return the pip proportion of _balance as _amount
        ├── when the pip proportion rounds down to zero
        │   └── it should return zero as _amount
        ├── when the pip value equals the denominator
        │   └── it should return _balance as _amount
        └── when using a known rounded down example
            └── it should return the hand computed floored proportion as _amount
